Doctrine's own `CursorPaginator` (ORM 3.7) has the same gap: `CursorWalker::buildCursorCondition()` compares the boundary with `col > :v`, so a `NULL` boundary ends the walk there too. A fix there would be worth having.

This PR is for ux-pagination as it is today: `DoctrineOrmAdapter` builds its own boundary predicate, so it doesn't benefit from a Doctrine fix until it moves onto Doctrine's paginator (#3898, waiting on doctrine/orm#12724). Once it does, the same handling needs to live in Doctrine.

